# Source: https://github.com/Illumina/canvas/issues/140
#   https://genome.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/help/bigWig.html
# Symptom: bedGraph file (4 columns: chrom, start, end, value) is not sorted
#   in case-sensitive lexicographic chromosome order required by bedGraphToBigWig.
#   The UCSC tool requires: `sort -k1,1 -k2,2n` with LC_COLLATE=C.
#   A locale-insensitive sort produces "chrM" before "chrX" on some systems
#   but "chrX" before "chrm" on others.  The specific error is:
#   "is not case-sensitive sorted at line N. Please use 'sort -k1,1 -k2,2n'
#   with LC_COLLATE=C, or bedSort and try again."
chr1	0	10000	0.5
chr2	0	10000	0.8
chrM	0	10000	1.0
chrX	0	10000	0.3
chr10	0	10000	0.6
